{
  "name": "How to Pick the Right Marble Finish for Your Bathroom",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Choosing the perfect marble finish for your bathroom involves a few key considerations to ensure both beauty and practicality. You'll want to think about the marble's porosity, its natural variations, and especially the finish – honed versus polished. Polished marble offers a high-gloss, reflective surface that really makes a statement, but it can be more slippery when wet, which is a big consideration for bathroom floors. Honed marble, on the other hand, has a matte or satin finish, offering better slip resistance and a more understated elegance. It's often a great choice for shower floors or high-traffic areas. Also, consider the tile size and if the product is explicitly suitable for wet-room or shower applications. It's always a good idea to order extra material, too, to account for any cuts or breakage during installation. A professional can walk you through these options and help you make the best choice for your specific bathroom and lifestyle, ensuring durability and safety.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
